msgid "Using OpenID Connect (OIDC) and Keycloak to centralize authorization"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Learn how to enable bearer token authorization in your Quarkus application "
"by using link:https://www.keycloak.org/docs/latest/authorization_services/"
"index.html[Keycloak Authorization Services] for secure access to protected "
"resources."
msgstr ""

msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Keycloak Authorization extension, `quarkus-keycloak-authorization`, "
"extends the OpenID Connect extension, `quarkus-oidc`, to provide advanced "
"authorization capabilities.\n"
"It features a policy enforcer that dynamically manages access to secured "
"resources.\n"
"Access is governed by permissions defined in Keycloak, supporting flexible "
"and dynamic Resource-Based Access Control (RBAC)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use the `quarkus-keycloak-authorization` extension only if you are using "
"Keycloak and the Keycloak Authorization Services feature is enabled in your "
"environment to handle authorization decisions."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are not using Keycloak, or if Keycloak is configured without the "
"Keycloak Authorization Services feature, use the `quarkus-oidc` extension "
"instead."
msgstr ""

msgid "How it works"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `quarkus-keycloak-authorization` extension centralizes authorization "
"responsibilities in Keycloak, enhancing security and simplifying application "
"maintenance:"
msgstr ""

msgid "It uses the `quarkus-oidc` extension to verify bearer tokens."
msgstr ""

msgid "It sends verified tokens to Keycloak Authorization Services."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It allows Keycloak to evaluate resource-based permissions dynamically by "
"using attributes such as resource name, identifier, or URI."
msgstr ""

msgid "By externalizing authorization decisions, you can:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Implement diverse access control strategies without modifying application "
"code."
msgstr ""

msgid "Reduce redeployment needs as security requirements evolve."
msgstr ""

msgid "Compatibility"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This extension is compatible only with Quarkus xref:security-oidc-bearer-"
"token-authentication.adoc[OIDC service applications].\n"
"It complements explicit mechanisms such as role-based access control with "
"dynamic authorization policies."
msgstr ""

msgid "Key Features"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Centralized Management**: Delegate authorization decisions to Keycloak for "
"consistent security policies across applications."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Dynamic Permissions**: Define access control dynamically by using resource "
"attributes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Simplified Maintenance**: Reduce the need to update and redeploy "
"applications when access policies change."
msgstr ""

msgid "Setting Up"
msgstr ""

msgid "Before using this extension, ensure the following:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Keycloak Authorization Services feature is enabled in your Keycloak instance."
""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Your Quarkus application includes the `quarkus-keycloak-authorization` "
"extension."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For detailed steps, see the xref:security-oidc-bearer-token-authentication."
"adoc[OIDC Bearer Token Authentication] guide."
msgstr ""

msgid "Additional resources"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To learn more about Keycloak Authorization Services and the policy enforcer, "
"visit the official documentation:\n"
"https://www.keycloak.org/docs/latest/authorization_services/index."
"html#_enforcer_overview[Keycloak Authorization Services Documentation]."
msgstr ""

