msgid "Architecture"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This example demonstrates a simple microservice setup with two protected "
"endpoints:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`/api/users/me`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`/api/admin`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Token-based access control"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Access to these endpoints is controlled by using bearer tokens.\n"
"To gain access, the following conditions must be met:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Valid token**: The token must have a correct signature, a valid expiration "
"date, and the appropriate audience."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Trust**: The microservice must trust the issuing Keycloak server."
msgstr ""

msgid "The bearer tokens issued by the Keycloak server serve as:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**User identifiers**: Indicating the subject (user) for whom the token was "
"issued."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Client references**: Identifying the client application acting on behalf "
"of the user, per OAuth 2.0 Authorization Server standards."
msgstr ""

msgid "Endpoints and access policies"
msgstr ""

msgid "For `/api/users/me`:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Access policy**: Open to users with a valid bearer token and the `user` "
"role."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Response**: Returns user details as a JSON object derived from the token."
msgstr ""

msgid "For `/api/admin`:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Access policy*: Restricted to users with a valid bearer token and the "
"`admin` role."
msgstr ""

msgid "Decoupled authorization"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This example highlights the use of role-based access control (RBAC) policies "
"to protect resources.\n"
"Key points include:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Policy flexibility*: Keycloak supports various policy types, such as "
"attribute-based and custom policies, enabling fine-grained control."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Decoupled application logic*: Authorization policies are managed entirely "
"by Keycloak, allowing your application to focus on its core functionality."
msgstr ""

msgid "Solution"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We recommend that you follow the instructions in the next sections and "
"create the application step by step.\n"
"However, you can go right to the completed example."
